WEBVTT

00:00.008 --> 00:35.166
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:09.243 --> 00:11.545
(dark music)

00:32.866 --> 00:35.636
(match striking)

00:44.178 --> 00:46.680
(upbeat music)

01:01.562 --> 01:02.663
- There's a fine line between
the things

01:03.131 --> 01:05.866
we choose to remember and
those we choose to forget.

01:06.734 --> 01:09.069
Memories are like incomplete
stories in that way.

01:10.204 --> 01:14.508
And the one I'm gonna tell you
is about love, loss, family,

01:15.676 --> 01:17.711
and some pretty fucking
bad decision-making.

01:19.147 --> 01:21.782
(upbeat music continues)

01:21.882 --> 01:23.217
This is a cautionary tale

01:23.317 --> 01:25.486
about a girl who got dealt a
shitty hand

01:25.586 --> 01:27.655
and tried to do something about
it.

01:27.755 --> 01:29.557
I know, I know.

01:29.657 --> 01:31.525
You get what you get
and you don't get upset.

01:32.593 --> 01:35.163
Well, I'm upset.

01:35.263 --> 01:37.165
(gun firing)

01:37.265 --> 01:38.766
Let me start from the beginning.

01:46.207 --> 01:48.509
- [Speaker 1] Oh my gosh, there
she is.

01:48.609 --> 01:49.910
[Speaker 2] Say hi, girls.

01:50.744 --> 01:52.780
What are you doing.

01:53.414 --> 01:55.949
- [Fox] My sister Spooky
and I were inseparable.

01:56.049 --> 01:58.018
But then Dad T-boned an 18
wheeler

01:58.118 --> 02:00.053
and everything went to shit
after that.

02:01.389 --> 02:03.824
Mom's casual alcoholism turned
into

02:03.924 --> 02:05.959
a not so casual drug problem,

02:06.059 --> 02:08.829
and suddenly I became
public enemy number one.

02:10.298 --> 02:12.466
Mom, stop! You can't keep doing
this.

02:12.566 --> 02:14.635
[Mom] Don't touch that.

02:14.735 --> 02:15.669
[Fox] Please, Mom!

02:15.769 --> 02:17.104
[Mom] Get the fuck out!

02:17.205 --> 02:19.139
I said get the fuck outta my
house!

02:19.240 --> 02:20.508
Fine!

02:20.608 --> 02:21.642
(door slamming)

02:21.742 --> 02:22.910
I can't stay here anymore.

02:23.711 --> 02:24.512
I'm done.

02:27.948 --> 02:29.082
Where are you gonna go?

02:30.150 --> 02:30.984
[Fox] I'm not sure.

02:33.887 --> 02:35.088
I can't keep fighting with her.

02:36.324 --> 02:38.158
(soft music playing distantly)

02:38.259 --> 02:39.627
[Spooky] But what about me?

02:41.462 --> 02:44.665
(soft music continues)

02:47.501 --> 02:48.101
You.

02:51.639 --> 02:52.206
You,

02:53.841 --> 02:56.477
could have this whole
room all to yourself.

03:00.848 --> 03:02.750
- [Spooky] I don't want you to
go.

03:02.850 --> 03:05.152
(tense music)

03:08.622 --> 03:10.524
There's food in the fridge,

03:10.624 --> 03:14.061
and that should last you a
couple of days.

03:14.161 --> 03:16.897
And then I put the number for
the pizza place by the phone.

03:19.032 --> 03:21.735
(dramatic music)

03:25.539 --> 03:27.341
- [Spooky] Promise you
won't forget about me?

03:28.676 --> 03:31.479
(sentimental music)

03:42.290 --> 03:43.757
[Fox] I'll be honest,

03:43.857 --> 03:45.659
I don't really remember much
after that.

03:48.061 --> 03:51.765
(sentimental music continues)

03:57.170 --> 04:00.508
That is, until she came along.

04:01.909 --> 04:04.845
Goldie, my first love.

04:05.979 --> 04:07.080
Hi, honey.

04:07.180 --> 04:10.117
(soft funky music)

04:16.524 --> 04:18.526
You look like you could
use a little bit of help.

04:22.195 --> 04:25.132
- [Fox] Some might call this
the beginning of the end.

04:25.232 --> 04:29.937
(engine revving)
(rock music)

04:31.572 --> 04:35.409
But for a minute there, it was
glorious.

04:35.509 --> 04:37.811
(rock music)

05:00.768 --> 05:02.035
Ever love someone so much,

05:02.135 --> 05:03.771
you'd follow them straight into
hell?

05:05.873 --> 05:06.974
Yeah, me too.

05:08.275 --> 05:12.380
("Fox on the Run" by Sweet)

05:12.480 --> 05:15.115
(door slamming)

05:16.884 --> 05:18.552
See, the thing about dating a
drug dealer

05:18.652 --> 05:20.854
is that they're always
looking for the next payday.

05:23.323 --> 05:28.429
* I don't wanna know your name

05:28.796 --> 05:32.666
* 'Cause you don't look the same
*

05:33.834 --> 05:35.268
- [Fox] And nothing's ever
enough.

05:39.840 --> 05:43.511
* You think you got a pretty
face *

05:43.611 --> 05:47.548
* But the rest of you is out of
place *

05:47.648 --> 05:51.652
* You looked all right before

05:51.752 --> 05:55.255
- [Fox] And if you're
making money on one vice,

05:55.355 --> 05:57.290
might as well make money on all
of them.

06:00.127 --> 06:03.864
("Fox on the Run" continues)

06:12.473 --> 06:13.941
Here you go, honey.

06:14.041 --> 06:15.943
- [Fox] Sure, it looks like a
party.

06:16.043 --> 06:17.210
Get in there.

06:17.310 --> 06:18.546
[Fox] But it stops being fun

06:18.646 --> 06:20.147
when you can't get off the ride.

06:24.051 --> 06:24.885
That's my girl.

06:27.287 --> 06:32.325
* You, you talk about just every
band *

06:32.460 --> 06:36.930
* But the names you drop are
second-hand *

06:38.632 --> 06:40.734
- But then last night, I saw
her.

06:42.002 --> 06:43.036
It was my little sister.

06:43.971 --> 06:45.439
(glass smashing)

06:45.539 --> 06:48.241
It was Spooky.

06:48.341 --> 06:49.743
- Where you going?
- Let go of me!

06:49.843 --> 06:50.678
Spooky!

06:52.846 --> 06:53.981
Spooky!

06:54.081 --> 06:54.915
Spooky!

06:56.316 --> 06:59.119
(people shouting)

07:00.554 --> 07:01.689
Spooky! Spooky!

07:02.756 --> 07:04.424
Spooky! Spooky! Spooky!

07:05.926 --> 07:07.394
And that's when I knew,

07:07.495 --> 07:09.362
I was gonna get back
to her no matter what.

07:12.700 --> 07:15.869
Now, getting out of here
unnoticed wasn't gonna be easy.

07:17.771 --> 07:18.939
(light music)

07:19.106 --> 07:22.042
Oh, didn't I mention, it was a
full house?

07:23.376 --> 07:25.445
That's Crystal, the bleeding
heart.

07:27.548 --> 07:30.017
And that's Minx, the hothead.

07:30.117 --> 07:31.585
(banging on table)

07:31.685 --> 07:35.523
Good people that lost
their way. Sound familiar?

07:35.623 --> 07:38.425
Neither have family, so they
took to this one pretty quick.

07:39.627 --> 07:43.163
Then there's Ricky and
Domino, the bruiser twins.

07:43.263 --> 07:44.832
They've done Goldie's dirty work

07:44.932 --> 07:47.034
ever since she made their
pervy daddy disappear.

07:47.134 --> 07:49.436
(Ricky laughing)

07:49.537 --> 07:50.938
Those guys can eat a dick.

07:52.105 --> 07:54.141
(upbeat music)

07:54.241 --> 07:55.843
See, Goldie had no one,

07:55.943 --> 07:58.278
so she collected all of us
like little fucking dolls,

07:58.378 --> 08:00.413
to keep locked up in her little
dollhouse.

08:03.784 --> 08:04.918
And she'll fight hard

08:05.118 --> 08:08.121
and she'll fight dirty
to keep what's hers.

08:08.221 --> 08:10.858
(dramatic music)

08:25.105 --> 08:26.206
I love you.

08:30.143 --> 08:31.344
Okay, let's eat.

08:36.349 --> 08:37.050
How you feeling, Boss?

08:37.150 --> 08:38.719
Fantastic.

08:40.921 --> 08:43.691
Barring our little
whoopsies from last night.

08:44.692 --> 08:46.994
Turns out the juice was worth
the squeeze,

08:47.094 --> 08:50.564
and we are on the precipice
of very lucrative deal.

08:50.664 --> 08:53.834
This time next week, we
will have a real pool.

08:55.202 --> 08:59.472
My dad always said that you
can turn any hand into gold.

09:00.507 --> 09:01.809
Just depends on how you play it.

09:03.010 --> 09:05.746
And, well, doesn't hurt
to know the dealer.

09:08.015 --> 09:09.249
To my old man,

09:11.151 --> 09:13.420
who would be rolling over in his
grave

09:13.520 --> 09:14.655
if he could see me now.

09:16.990 --> 09:19.727
Never underestimate the power
of being underestimated.

09:19.827 --> 09:22.162
- Or how many dime bags
it takes to fill a pool.

09:24.798 --> 09:27.400
(Crystal coughing)

09:27.500 --> 09:28.335
What was that?

09:31.739 --> 09:32.505
A joke.

09:40.047 --> 09:41.782
- Do you think that
you can do a better job

09:41.882 --> 09:43.450
at providing for us, is that it?

09:49.422 --> 09:50.257
Articulate.

09:52.392 --> 09:53.226
No.

09:56.496 --> 09:58.498
Well, I guess we know Fox

09:58.598 --> 10:00.934
isn't the funny one of the
group.

10:01.034 --> 10:03.536
(group laughing)

10:05.372 --> 10:08.608
(banging on table)

10:08.709 --> 10:11.111
(tense music)

10:15.348 --> 10:16.850
(dog barking)

10:16.950 --> 10:18.585
(traffic passing)

10:18.686 --> 10:21.154
(tense music)

10:29.096 --> 10:30.898
- [Police Officer]
Breaker, what's your 20?

10:31.932 --> 10:34.868
- 912, suspicious person
on scene, standing by.

10:34.968 --> 10:35.969
[Police Officer] Need you back

10:36.203 --> 10:37.938
at the station to meet the new
recruit.

10:38.038 --> 10:39.773
- You mean the brown-noser?

10:39.873 --> 10:41.574
- [Police Officer] Breaker, be
nice.

10:42.642 --> 10:43.777
Well, I guess it makes sense

10:43.877 --> 10:46.446
you wanted her to learn from the
best.

10:46.546 --> 10:47.580
- [Police Officer] That's the
spirit.

10:49.049 --> 10:50.317
(Breaker chuckling)

10:50.483 --> 10:53.186
- [Breaker] Good old
Goldie, always on the money.

10:55.823 --> 10:58.258
(tense music)

11:00.427 --> 11:00.994
Let's go to work.

11:03.931 --> 11:06.199
(rock music)

11:15.008 --> 11:15.843
Shit.

11:20.147 --> 11:21.581
Howdy.

11:21.681 --> 11:22.515
You're not Rocco, are you?

11:23.350 --> 11:25.552
- I'm gonna need you to pass
me your keys nice and slow.

11:28.121 --> 11:28.688
Thank you.

11:30.323 --> 11:31.191
Why don't you hop out of the
car?

11:38.866 --> 11:39.733
How old are you?

11:41.334 --> 11:42.269
I'm 16.

11:42.369 --> 11:42.970
Jesus Christ.

11:44.471 --> 11:46.273
- Look, I got my license
and registration inside.

11:46.373 --> 11:47.207
Cool.

11:51.011 --> 11:51.879
- All right, all right. This
ain't my car.

11:52.479 --> 11:54.748
This is my cousin's car,
and he's doing some time.

11:55.783 --> 11:57.517
And he just said to look after
it.

11:57.617 --> 11:59.452
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait.

11:59.552 --> 12:00.687
I know this looks bad,
but I swear, I swear.

12:00.788 --> 12:02.022
I've never done this before.

12:02.222 --> 12:04.191
Please, just please let
me go, don't do anything.

12:04.291 --> 12:06.293
(gun firing)

12:06.393 --> 12:08.661
(tense music)

12:27.881 --> 12:31.218
(tense music continues)

12:39.827 --> 12:40.627
Fox?

12:42.930 --> 12:43.696
Fox?

12:44.998 --> 12:46.166
Come here.

12:46.266 --> 12:46.900
Come here.

12:48.568 --> 12:50.503
Let me look at you, let's see.

12:50.603 --> 12:52.139
Oh, sweetheart.

12:54.107 --> 12:55.876
Oh, you took a bad tumble.

12:58.678 --> 13:00.713
That was too hard, I'm so sorry.

13:03.683 --> 13:05.718
I just don't understand
what's gotten into you.

13:07.120 --> 13:08.121
Ever since last night.

13:08.221 --> 13:09.056
Spooky!

13:13.626 --> 13:15.362
I just wanted to talk to her.

13:15.462 --> 13:17.297
- Oh, sweetheart, that wasn't
anybody.

13:19.732 --> 13:20.800
You trust me, don't you?

13:23.736 --> 13:26.739
We're gonna make you all
better, okay? I promise.

13:29.042 --> 13:29.843
(Goldie humming)

13:29.943 --> 13:33.280
(camera shutter clicking)

13:33.380 --> 13:36.016
(shutter clicking)

13:46.226 --> 13:48.761
(water spraying)

13:51.131 --> 13:56.169
- [Radio Host] All your
most intimate fantasies.

13:57.170 --> 13:58.471
- You ever think about getting
outta here?

14:00.273 --> 14:00.840
Why?

14:03.076 --> 14:04.777
- I mean, don't you want more
than this?

14:07.580 --> 14:08.949
- Everything I want is right
here.

14:14.487 --> 14:16.423
(zipper zipping)

14:16.523 --> 14:19.692
(dog barking)

14:19.792 --> 14:23.463
(officers chattering on radio)

14:29.970 --> 14:31.138
(door closing)

14:31.604 --> 14:35.208
- Breaker, our new recruit
wanted to see you in action.

14:35.308 --> 14:39.346
Officer Kelly Corbett, former
SFPD. We're lucky to have her.

14:41.114 --> 14:42.749
- Sergeant Breaker, it's
so nice to meet you.

14:42.849 --> 14:44.351
I've heard a lot about you.

14:44.451 --> 14:45.252
Yeah.

14:46.786 --> 14:48.188
So, what happened here?

14:48.288 --> 14:49.923
- Well, I witnessed the perp
dealing,

14:50.023 --> 14:51.959
so I drew on him, told him not
to move.

14:52.059 --> 14:55.628
He came at me with a knife
when I was searching the car.

14:55.728 --> 14:57.530
Left me no other choice but to
shoot him.

14:58.665 --> 15:01.068
(tense music)

15:20.753 --> 15:22.655
There's nothing here.

15:22.755 --> 15:24.024
- That's how I found it, short
stack.

15:26.526 --> 15:27.094
Don't do that.

15:29.762 --> 15:30.730
Corbett, let's go

15:32.832 --> 15:35.168
meet with the other team
members.

15:35.268 --> 15:37.704
(lid closing)

15:41.341 --> 15:43.176
- Look forward to working
together, Sergeant.

15:43.276 --> 15:44.077
Yeah.

15:47.047 --> 15:48.781
Not for fucking long.

15:51.851 --> 15:54.454
(phone ringing)

15:56.223 --> 15:56.889
Yep?

16:03.530 --> 16:04.231
Breaker?

16:05.532 --> 16:06.333
It's done.

16:06.533 --> 16:07.767
[Goldie] Good. Kept it tidy?

16:07.867 --> 16:09.669
Not exactly. One casualty.

16:09.769 --> 16:10.637
Sloppy.

16:12.239 --> 16:14.307
- [Breaker] Well, I had
to given the size of it.

16:14.407 --> 16:16.609
Hmm. How much are we talking?

16:18.611 --> 16:20.580
- Enough snow to cancel school
for a year.

16:24.384 --> 16:28.721
- Huh. Well, we'll see you
tonight then, Billy Boy.

16:28.821 --> 16:30.790
I'll put the girls down early.

16:30.890 --> 16:31.558
Yeah.

16:31.658 --> 16:34.294
(pensive music)

16:39.466 --> 16:41.834
(rock music)

16:52.179 --> 16:55.882
(girls yelling and laughing)

16:57.417 --> 17:00.487
(rock music continues)

17:01.621 --> 17:05.158
(girls yelling and laughing)

17:09.996 --> 17:10.830
My girls,

17:13.133 --> 17:14.834
we have a little celebrating to
do.

17:19.372 --> 17:21.808
(tense music)

17:24.877 --> 17:27.314
(owl hooting)

17:28.515 --> 17:31.584
(eerie music)

17:31.684 --> 17:32.519
Never forget,

17:35.655 --> 17:36.856
our family,

17:38.325 --> 17:39.826
is thicker than blood.

17:44.464 --> 17:47.300
(eerie music)

17:47.400 --> 17:48.067
I love you.

17:51.171 --> 17:53.573
(tense music)

17:55.142 --> 17:58.245
Thick, thick, thicker thank
blood.

17:58.345 --> 17:59.479
Thicker than blood.

17:59.579 --> 18:00.813
Thicker than blood.

18:00.913 --> 18:03.216
(rock music)

18:10.022 --> 18:12.692
(girls talking)

18:17.897 --> 18:20.300
(tense music)

18:35.615 --> 18:39.051
(girls hooting and yelling)

18:43.856 --> 18:45.458
[Spooky] Catch me!

18:47.194 --> 18:47.994
Spooky!

18:50.863 --> 18:52.399
Spooky, I'm coming!

18:54.234 --> 18:56.769
(upbeat music)

18:57.770 --> 18:58.838
Spooky!

18:58.938 --> 19:01.140
(pop music)

19:08.381 --> 19:11.951
(camera shutter clicking)

19:12.051 --> 19:14.854
(eerie music)

19:14.954 --> 19:17.357
(car running)

19:23.630 --> 19:26.366
(car door closing)

19:26.466 --> 19:28.701
I'd recognize that stupid hat
anywhere.

19:30.069 --> 19:32.672
Breaker, Goldie's bagman.

19:34.073 --> 19:36.909
They've been burying money
in the ground for years,

19:37.009 --> 19:39.145
and I happen to know
exactly where they stash it.

19:41.281 --> 19:43.616
(rock music)

19:54.961 --> 19:58.030
(rock music continues)

19:58.798 --> 20:01.534
(cars shuffling)

20:07.139 --> 20:08.908
Ah, Billy Boy.

20:09.008 --> 20:11.311
(rock music)

20:21.621 --> 20:24.156
Oh. Fuck the small talk, I
guess.

20:25.858 --> 20:26.959
Just open it.

20:27.059 --> 20:30.029
(zipper unzipping)

20:31.698 --> 20:32.665
- Holy-

20:33.300 --> 20:35.167
- Half a million. Even
split, right down the middle.

20:38.237 --> 20:41.374
- And when did you become such
a greedy little thumbsucker?

20:41.474 --> 20:42.909
I made it happen, didn't I?

20:43.009 --> 20:44.010
On my tip.

20:47.046 --> 20:49.582
You know, if I didn't know any
better,

20:52.519 --> 20:54.454
I'd think you were
getting ready to retire.

20:55.522 --> 20:57.156
- Everything we've done before
this

20:57.256 --> 20:59.125
is child's play in comparison.

20:59.225 --> 21:01.394
- I've got people to feed,
Billy.

21:01.494 --> 21:02.862
And I'm risking everything.

21:04.230 --> 21:06.633
(tense music)

21:20.279 --> 21:21.414
Okay, Sarge.

21:23.182 --> 21:24.517
Just this once.

21:24.617 --> 21:25.652
50-50.

21:28.054 --> 21:29.055
Because you deserve it.

21:33.426 --> 21:35.495
We gotta move it in one clip,
though.

21:35.595 --> 21:38.331
Set up a game night. Let
the gangs do what they do.

21:38.431 --> 21:41.100
Doc Rogers rides with the trust.

21:41.200 --> 21:42.935
Ugly motherfucker, but he's
clean.

21:43.035 --> 21:45.204
Fine. Just lemme know when.

21:45.304 --> 21:47.740
(dark music)

21:49.909 --> 21:51.344
Doc, Goldie.

21:52.479 --> 21:56.215
I got a big one for you.

21:56.315 --> 21:59.251
I'll see you Friday night.
Thanks, Doc.

22:00.219 --> 22:01.020
Voila.

22:03.423 --> 22:05.792
Now, how about a smile?

22:05.892 --> 22:06.693
Yeah.

22:08.928 --> 22:10.597
Your cut from the last job.

22:12.832 --> 22:14.100
Pleasure as always.

22:17.003 --> 22:19.271
(dark music)

22:23.009 --> 22:26.546
(car starting)

22:26.646 --> 22:27.279
Stash it.

22:28.648 --> 22:31.050
(tense music)

22:38.958 --> 22:42.995
(ATV attempting to start)

22:43.095 --> 22:45.965
(high-tension music)

23:10.857 --> 23:13.359
(thug whistling)

23:18.631 --> 23:21.100
(tense music)

23:21.200 --> 23:23.836
(door creaking)

23:27.039 --> 23:29.341
(door closing)

23:34.180 --> 23:37.450
(owl hooting)

23:37.550 --> 23:40.286
(thug whistling)

23:43.490 --> 23:45.892
(eerie music)

23:51.531 --> 23:54.066
(ATV starting)

24:02.208 --> 24:03.042
Hey.

24:10.950 --> 24:12.985
(tense music)

24:13.085 --> 24:13.953
Where's Fox?

24:15.855 --> 24:17.089
Hello?

24:17.189 --> 24:18.991
Where's Fox?

24:19.091 --> 24:21.494
(tense music)

24:26.766 --> 24:29.101
(rock music)

24:48.888 --> 24:49.656
Fuck!

24:52.091 --> 24:54.426
(rock music)

25:12.244 --> 25:15.347
(rock music continues)

25:26.025 --> 25:28.460
(pensive music)

25:32.431 --> 25:34.901
(car rumbling)

25:45.978 --> 25:46.879
(knocking on door)

25:46.979 --> 25:47.814
Spooky?

25:54.386 --> 25:55.221
Spook?

26:00.893 --> 26:03.329
(soft music)

26:07.634 --> 26:08.500
Hello?

26:17.844 --> 26:18.510
Spooky?

26:22.682 --> 26:24.550
- [Mom] You don't think I feel
you

26:24.651 --> 26:25.718
- judging me all the time.
- Mom, stop.

26:25.818 --> 26:27.519
- [Mom] Little miss fucking
perfect.

26:30.522 --> 26:32.959
(soft music)

26:48.875 --> 26:53.012
- Oh, shit, this isn't
Spooky's.

26:53.112 --> 26:55.948
(dramatic music)

27:10.196 --> 27:12.965
Remember when I mentioned some
pretty bad decision-making?

27:14.566 --> 27:15.434
Well,

27:16.202 --> 27:17.636
there's more.

27:17.737 --> 27:20.339
(upbeat music)

27:22.641 --> 27:26.312
- No, no, no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no.

27:26.412 --> 27:27.579
Where the fuck is the money?

27:29.081 --> 27:31.784
Shit!

27:34.954 --> 27:37.423
- Oh, come on. Pick up the
fucking phone.

27:38.958 --> 27:41.360
(tense music)

27:43.830 --> 27:46.465
(phone ringing)

27:49.135 --> 27:51.871
(phone ringing)

27:51.971 --> 27:54.640
(tense music)

27:54.741 --> 27:57.543
(cards shuffling)

27:58.477 --> 28:00.780
(rock music)

28:04.116 --> 28:06.318
(phone ringing)

28:06.418 --> 28:09.822
(chatter on police radio)

28:11.457 --> 28:13.625
- Hey, this may go down
smoother.

28:16.128 --> 28:19.498
(Breaker slurping)

28:19.598 --> 28:21.133
Did I do something to upset you?

28:23.770 --> 28:24.570
Nope.

28:26.672 --> 28:28.274
The Frogman case up north,

28:28.374 --> 28:30.910
you must have been
really proud of yourself.

28:31.010 --> 28:33.545
Brave Officer testifies against
her own.

28:34.613 --> 28:35.782
Nothing like getting transferred

28:35.882 --> 28:37.549
to a shithole town like this to
reward you

28:37.649 --> 28:39.551
for your good behavior, huh?

28:44.390 --> 28:46.859
- Look, I don't wanna be here
anymore than you want me here.

28:46.959 --> 28:49.728
- Finally, something we can
agree on.

28:51.197 --> 28:52.231
You gonna get that?

28:52.364 --> 28:55.001
- Nah, just the old ball and
chain.

28:59.371 --> 29:01.740
(radio chatter)

29:03.642 --> 29:04.643
Where the hell have you been?

29:04.743 --> 29:06.212
Doing my job?

29:06.412 --> 29:07.579
What the fuck is so important
that you keep blowing me up?

29:07.679 --> 29:09.281
Fox took the cargo and ran.

29:10.482 --> 29:12.051
- I'm sorry. What'd you just
say?

29:12.151 --> 29:15.221
- What about what I just
said? Didn't you understand?

29:15.321 --> 29:17.089
Are you fucking kidding me?

29:17.189 --> 29:18.724
How does that happen?

29:18.825 --> 29:21.260
Honestly, I laid this in your
lap.

29:21.360 --> 29:22.594
How do you lose it?

29:22.829 --> 29:25.064
I mean, it's not like
it's just a couple bricks.

29:25.164 --> 29:27.099
Goldie, you fucking incompetent
junkie.

29:27.199 --> 29:29.936
- Consider this an official
missing person's report.

29:30.036 --> 29:31.470
I don't fucking work for you.

29:31.570 --> 29:33.172
- Oh, that's funny because
the pictures I have

29:33.272 --> 29:36.108
of you snorting cocaine off
a hooker's ass say otherwise.

29:42.281 --> 29:44.817
(upbeat music)

29:44.917 --> 29:47.253
- [Fox] So no Spooky,
and a bag full of blow.

29:47.353 --> 29:49.121
I had to stash the thing
somewhere,

29:49.221 --> 29:51.290
and there was only one safe
place I could think of.

29:52.558 --> 29:54.994
(light music)

30:13.079 --> 30:15.614
(light music)

30:23.622 --> 30:27.493
(gasping) Hi. Sorry.

30:27.593 --> 30:28.294
Sorry.

30:28.394 --> 30:30.062
You scared me.

30:30.162 --> 30:31.830
Sorry. Can I help you?

30:31.931 --> 30:35.301
Yeah, I was just looking for

30:35.401 --> 30:38.670
a locker to put my things in.

30:38.770 --> 30:40.106
Those are for customers only.

30:41.440 --> 30:42.341
Are you skating?

30:44.443 --> 30:46.212
No. No.

30:49.748 --> 30:50.549
But,

30:52.851 --> 30:55.221
I was hoping that

30:55.321 --> 30:56.522
maybe

30:56.622 --> 30:57.990
you

30:58.090 --> 30:58.790
could

31:01.293 --> 31:02.061
let me use it still.

31:05.631 --> 31:06.798
What's in the bag?

31:08.500 --> 31:10.369
Bricks of cocaine.

31:10.469 --> 31:13.105
(both laughing)

31:13.205 --> 31:13.805
Really funny.

31:16.542 --> 31:18.410
(bright instrumental music)

31:18.510 --> 31:21.380
(employee screaming)

31:26.718 --> 31:29.488
(copier running)

31:32.959 --> 31:33.859
- Hey Sarge, I just got a call
about the

31:33.960 --> 31:35.361
traffic light glitching on Main.

31:35.461 --> 31:37.964
I was gonna head out before
calling Traffic Control.

31:38.064 --> 31:39.331
- You know, Corbett, I got a
better idea.

31:39.465 --> 31:40.599
Why don't you stay here
and type up the report

31:40.699 --> 31:41.900
from my bust yesterday.

31:42.001 --> 31:43.402
- With all due respect, I'm not-

31:43.635 --> 31:46.538
- Isn't Frisco where they
invented these dumb machines?

31:46.638 --> 31:47.906
I bet you're a star on them.

31:48.007 --> 31:49.175
Maybe when you're done,

31:49.375 --> 31:51.777
you can help Pam type
up our archived cases.

31:51.877 --> 31:54.713
Women helping women. See,
I could be a feminist.

32:00.352 --> 32:02.921
(sinister music)

32:18.670 --> 32:19.471
Find the girl.

32:20.706 --> 32:21.540
Fox will come.

32:24.110 --> 32:26.878
(sinister music)

32:42.228 --> 32:43.129
- [Corbett] What kind of drug
dealer

32:43.429 --> 32:45.397
assaults an officer for an
eightball?

32:47.233 --> 32:49.901
(sinister music)

33:08.220 --> 33:10.922
(sinister music)

33:13.559 --> 33:16.928
(Pam clearing her throat)

33:21.733 --> 33:24.203
(eerie music)

33:24.303 --> 33:27.173
Pam, right? Kelly Corbett.

33:27.273 --> 33:28.040
I know.

33:28.140 --> 33:28.974
Of course.

33:29.141 --> 33:30.742
I wasn't sure since, you know,

33:30.842 --> 33:32.378
we didn't have proper
introduction.

33:32.478 --> 33:34.313
- What can I do for you,
Officer?

33:34.446 --> 33:35.013
Yeah.

33:36.448 --> 33:38.217
What can you tell me about the
Sergeant?

33:40.619 --> 33:41.820
- Well, he's got the highest
rate

33:41.920 --> 33:43.455
of closed cases north of
Sacramento.

33:45.023 --> 33:45.957
- [Kelly] With a record like
that,

33:46.158 --> 33:48.194
he must be a very gifted
detective.

33:49.027 --> 33:50.962
- [Pam] Well, the Captain
certainly thinks so.

33:52.464 --> 33:53.665
[Kelly] And you don't?

33:53.765 --> 33:55.934
[Pam] I didn't say that.

33:56.034 --> 33:58.337
- [Kelly] Huh? Is there
anything else you can share?

33:59.771 --> 34:02.208
(door closing)

34:02.308 --> 34:04.776
(dark music)

34:04.876 --> 34:06.512
Just a word of advice.

34:10.182 --> 34:12.017
I suggest you tread lightly.

34:12.118 --> 34:16.054
Nothing is more dangerous than
a man who's been humiliated.

34:16.155 --> 34:18.557
(tense music)

34:30.736 --> 34:32.538
(knocking on door)

34:32.638 --> 34:33.372
Housekeeping.

34:34.840 --> 34:37.243
(rock music)

34:46.752 --> 34:48.454
Man, what the fuck?

34:48.554 --> 34:49.955
You're always such a buzzkill.

34:51.590 --> 34:53.892
Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa. That's her.

34:53.992 --> 34:54.926
That's her, that's her, that's
her.

34:55.026 --> 34:56.895
THat's the girl from the party.

34:56.995 --> 34:57.729
Shit shit. That's her, that's
her.

34:57.829 --> 34:58.530
Pull over. Pull over.

35:08.340 --> 35:10.642
(dark music)

35:13.078 --> 35:16.047
(shutter clicking)

35:22.754 --> 35:23.589
Want some?

35:32.598 --> 35:33.232
What's your name?

35:34.466 --> 35:37.068
(pensive music)

35:42.641 --> 35:43.409
I'll tell you what,

35:44.910 --> 35:45.977
you tell me your name

35:47.313 --> 35:49.215
and I'll help get you outta
here.

35:49.315 --> 35:50.349
I'll even let you drive.

35:52.651 --> 35:55.287
(pensive music)

35:59.758 --> 36:01.693
(door closing)

36:01.793 --> 36:02.961
That's a pretty name.

36:04.830 --> 36:05.664
I hate it.

36:07.266 --> 36:09.201
So change it. Who cares?

36:11.270 --> 36:12.571
Who's gonna know?

36:12.671 --> 36:15.441
(dramatic music)

36:24.483 --> 36:26.952
(car revving)

36:37.429 --> 36:39.831
(car running)

36:42.934 --> 36:45.404
(Spooky screaming)

36:45.504 --> 36:46.872
Spooky! Spooky!

36:46.972 --> 36:48.740
(tires squealing)

36:48.840 --> 36:49.775
Spooky!

36:49.875 --> 36:52.143
(Fox crashing)

37:07.058 --> 37:10.662
(faint middle eastern music)

37:13.399 --> 37:14.600
What's going on?

37:16.835 --> 37:17.536
Where am I?

37:18.837 --> 37:20.071
You're okay.

37:22.641 --> 37:23.742
Why am I here?

37:23.975 --> 37:26.878
- Well, you kind of
ate the hood of my car.

37:26.978 --> 37:30.081
But don't worry, your
money maker's still intact.

37:30.181 --> 37:32.183
- Who are you?
- Me? I'm Frankie.

37:33.585 --> 37:34.720
[Fox] Meet Frankie,

37:34.920 --> 37:37.589
a delusional nut job with a
heart of gold.

37:37.689 --> 37:38.757
Couldn't find an ID on you,

37:38.857 --> 37:40.992
so my options were a little
limited.

37:41.092 --> 37:43.261
I thought about calling the
cops,

37:43.362 --> 37:46.665
but that doesn't really
go well for a Jane Doe.

37:46.765 --> 37:51.136
Oh God. I have to get my
sister, they're gonna kill her.

37:52.504 --> 37:55.807
- Relax. Let me, I'm
gonna get you some water.

37:55.907 --> 37:57.142
I'll be right back.

38:00.846 --> 38:03.214
(Fox groaning)

38:07.553 --> 38:10.221
(pensive music)

38:30.909 --> 38:31.743
Come on.

38:32.878 --> 38:34.480
A goddamn stalker.

38:37.383 --> 38:40.318
- Wow, dude. You're like
super, super pretty man.

38:40.419 --> 38:42.153
Sir.

38:42.253 --> 38:45.391
Thank you. Can you describe the
girl?

38:45.491 --> 38:46.992
- Which one?
- Either.

38:47.092 --> 38:48.293
Sure, sure, sure, sure.

38:48.394 --> 38:50.295
So, the one running down the
street.

38:50.396 --> 38:52.163
Yeah, she was, she was pretty
hot.

38:52.263 --> 38:54.332
And then the one that hit her,

38:54.433 --> 38:55.266
she was pretty easy on the eyes
too.

38:55.434 --> 38:57.703
She had this crazy like, yeah.

38:57.803 --> 39:00.739
And, and the universe of
purple, I would say hair.

39:00.839 --> 39:01.807
Purple hair.

39:01.907 --> 39:03.475
- Yeah.
- Anything else?

39:03.575 --> 39:06.311
- Oh yeah, she was, she
was crazy strong too.

39:06.412 --> 39:07.846
She carried that blonde chick

39:07.946 --> 39:09.415
like she was a cutout cardboard
man.

39:09.515 --> 39:11.550
- Blonde girl, can you
describe her height?

39:11.650 --> 39:13.051
Short hair, long hair, anything
like that.

39:13.151 --> 39:14.152
- She was like-
- Hey.

39:16.488 --> 39:18.056
Hey Sarge.

39:18.156 --> 39:19.190
What are you doing here?

39:19.357 --> 39:21.226
- I got a call up about a hit
and run.

39:21.326 --> 39:22.160
Usual.

39:23.929 --> 39:25.063
Can you describe the car?

39:25.163 --> 39:26.532
Hell yeah.

39:26.632 --> 39:29.668
It was one of those galaxy
blue, like Cutlasses.

39:29.768 --> 39:33.405
Okay. Oldsmobile blue Cutlass.

39:33.505 --> 39:34.339
[Counterman] Yeah.

39:35.173 --> 39:37.242
- Did you catch any of the
numbers on the license plate?

39:37.943 --> 39:39.578
- I think there's like a four in
it.

39:39.678 --> 39:40.311
Thanks.

39:48.820 --> 39:51.356
Oh, one more thing. Do you
recognize her?

39:51.457 --> 39:55.360
- [Counterman] Yeah, yeah. See,
I told you, she's hot, man.

39:55.461 --> 39:57.729
- Great. Thanks a lot.
- Have a slice day.

39:57.829 --> 39:59.364
- Hey Pam, can you pull all DMV
records

39:59.465 --> 40:01.467
of people who own a blue
Oldsmobile...

40:01.567 --> 40:03.368
- Hey.
- ...Cutlass in the county.

40:03.469 --> 40:04.603
Hey, I'm talking to you.

40:06.371 --> 40:07.739
Where are you going?

40:07.839 --> 40:09.641
To find your missing girl.

40:09.741 --> 40:11.710
- Let's get something
straight, short stack.

40:11.810 --> 40:15.046
This is my case. Look
around, this is my town.

40:15.146 --> 40:16.347
Just trying to do my job.

40:18.484 --> 40:19.518
How noble of you.

40:22.888 --> 40:24.355
I don't think you understand me.

40:25.691 --> 40:28.393
You do what I let you do. Got
it?

40:28.494 --> 40:31.597
(sinister music)

40:31.697 --> 40:32.731
Since you're here,

40:32.864 --> 40:34.399
we might as well put you to good
use.

40:34.500 --> 40:35.300
Come with me.

40:38.069 --> 40:39.070
Not that way.

40:41.006 --> 40:43.809
- I'll go first. Frankie
DeFranco, combat medic.

40:44.876 --> 40:49.147
Well, actually I should
say ex-combat medic.

40:49.247 --> 40:51.650
I saw some crazy

40:51.750 --> 40:52.751
shit and

40:54.620 --> 40:56.588
I don't know, sometimes I still
do.

40:56.688 --> 40:57.656
Yeah.

40:57.889 --> 41:01.326
- Anytime I hear the tick, tick,
tick.

41:01.426 --> 41:02.293
It's like,

41:04.596 --> 41:09.334
but, fun fact, sugar
always brings me back.

41:09.434 --> 41:12.804
So anyways, I got discharged on
account

41:12.904 --> 41:15.874
of seeing some stuff that
they told me I didn't see.

41:15.974 --> 41:18.644
So now I'm back here just until,

41:18.744 --> 41:20.712
you know, I find a place of my
own.

41:20.812 --> 41:22.948
So that's me.

41:25.717 --> 41:26.417
Your turn.

41:33.892 --> 41:38.530
Goldie is going to kill your
sister, is that the story?

41:38.630 --> 41:40.699
- Wait, what? How, how'd you
know?

41:40.799 --> 41:44.135
- You were mumbling her name
while you were knocked out, so.

41:45.336 --> 41:49.541
(gasping) Oh my God. Unless
Goldie is your sister.

41:51.677 --> 41:52.811
That's a long story.

41:54.813 --> 41:56.948
I love long stories.

42:00.185 --> 42:04.890
- So, about this missing girl,
you gonna tell me who she is?

42:04.990 --> 42:06.758
Just another gutter rat.

42:06.858 --> 42:08.560
So what's it to you?

42:08.660 --> 42:10.061
Just trying to do my job.

42:12.263 --> 42:14.432
- You know, there are smarter
ways to locate a vehicle.

42:14.532 --> 42:16.401
Calling me stupid, Frisco?

42:16.501 --> 42:19.738
(tires squealing)

42:19.838 --> 42:21.472
Looky looky here. You were
saying?

42:25.143 --> 42:25.977
Shit.

42:27.846 --> 42:30.081
- Hey Pam, how are we
doing on this DMV records?

42:31.783 --> 42:32.918
- [Pam] I pulled three and
counting.

42:33.018 --> 42:34.019
[Kelly] Copy that.

42:34.119 --> 42:35.453
(door closing)

42:35.553 --> 42:38.089
- [Frankie] Wow. So what's the
plan?

42:38.189 --> 42:40.458
- I mean, I have to go back for
my sister.

42:40.558 --> 42:44.262
- You do realize that Goldie
is baiting you, right?

42:44.362 --> 42:45.430
What choice do I have?

42:46.898 --> 42:51.069
(acoustic guitar music)

42:51.169 --> 42:52.871
I can think of a few.

42:56.541 --> 42:59.444
Welcome to Habibi headquarters.

43:06.484 --> 43:08.586
[Fox] Whoa.

43:08.687 --> 43:09.520
Holy shit.

43:10.488 --> 43:11.522
Pretty cool, huh?

43:15.260 --> 43:16.161
[Fox] Did you make these?

43:16.261 --> 43:18.396
No, my brother did.

43:18.496 --> 43:19.898
He's obsessed with martial arts.

43:19.998 --> 43:22.167
Well, he's not actually my
brother,

43:22.267 --> 43:23.969
but he practically is.

43:24.069 --> 43:25.036
His family took me in.

43:26.071 --> 43:26.938
Speak of the devil.

43:28.339 --> 43:29.474
Well, hello.

43:29.574 --> 43:31.977
Dylan, this is uh.

43:32.077 --> 43:33.078
Fox.

43:33.178 --> 43:34.445
And finally.

43:34.545 --> 43:36.114
Dylan.

43:36.214 --> 43:39.084
- [Fox] Action film fanatic
with a penchant for Stallone.

43:39.184 --> 43:40.618
Nice to meet you.

43:40.852 --> 43:42.420
- [Dispatch On Scanner] Injury
accident, 14th Street north.

43:42.520 --> 43:46.792
- So Dylan, my friend Fox is
in a little bit of a situation.

43:47.893 --> 43:48.727
What kind of a situation?

43:49.394 --> 43:52.030
- Think Aunty Entity,
lost tribe in Thunderdome,

43:52.130 --> 43:53.298
bow with commando.

43:54.866 --> 43:56.201
No shit.

43:56.301 --> 43:58.136
I fucking love Commando.

43:58.236 --> 43:59.070
What's Commando?

44:01.439 --> 44:03.041
- Listen.
- Oh, no, no.

44:03.141 --> 44:04.910
You know, we'll deal
with that. Look at me.

44:06.444 --> 44:09.948
High risk expedition, everything
we've been training for.

44:10.048 --> 44:11.516
You in?

44:11.616 --> 44:13.384
Yeah, I'm free. Let's do it.

44:13.484 --> 44:16.187
No, no. This isn't a game.

44:16.287 --> 44:19.791
I, I'm not, no one is in, and
I'm not taking you with me.

44:19.891 --> 44:21.359
- Listen lady, you will
not find two people

44:21.459 --> 44:22.660
more qualified than us.

44:22.761 --> 44:23.862
I don't even know you.

44:23.962 --> 44:25.596
It's fine. She's right.

44:26.564 --> 44:29.367
She doesn't know us or need us

44:30.902 --> 44:31.970
or any of our stuff.

44:34.405 --> 44:35.606
Good luck, I guess.

44:36.942 --> 44:39.210
So you have no problem finding
your sister

44:39.310 --> 44:42.113
and your friends all by
yourself.

44:45.516 --> 44:46.785
Why do you even wanna help me?

44:48.153 --> 44:51.289
- I'm a combat medic,
helping people's what I do.

44:52.490 --> 44:54.059
Plus I kind of owe you, the car.

44:55.626 --> 44:57.062
- [Dispatch On Scanner]
Searching for a blue

44:57.295 --> 45:00.565
Oldsmobile Cutlass for a hit
and run off I-99 headed east.

45:00.665 --> 45:02.700
Driver possibly armed.

45:02.801 --> 45:03.835
So what's it gonna be?

45:09.975 --> 45:11.076
Good choice.

45:11.176 --> 45:12.744
What now?

45:12.844 --> 45:16.982
- Now do what they do
in every action movie.

45:18.449 --> 45:20.852
- [Fox] Well, these two
are definitely a bad fit,

45:20.952 --> 45:23.088
but beggars can't be choosers.

45:23.188 --> 45:23.755
Fuck it.

45:26.124 --> 45:28.393
(soft music)

45:36.301 --> 45:37.102
Ha!

45:38.736 --> 45:39.570
What the fuck?

45:40.906 --> 45:43.541
(upbeat music)

45:45.877 --> 45:47.979
- All in the wrist, okay?
- Okay.

45:48.079 --> 45:49.781
Come, come on again.

45:53.318 --> 45:55.553
One, come, one two, come.

45:55.653 --> 45:58.256
(upbeat music)

45:59.724 --> 46:02.327
- The painkillers are really
kicking in.

46:02.427 --> 46:03.694
Elbow here. Boom.

46:08.333 --> 46:09.267
Okay, here.

46:09.367 --> 46:10.201
No, I got it this time.

46:10.335 --> 46:12.470
- Okay, go ahead.
- Mm-hm.

46:12.570 --> 46:14.739
Shit!

46:14.840 --> 46:16.274
Stash it.

46:16.374 --> 46:18.676
(car revving)

46:18.776 --> 46:20.478
Come on, one two. Yes.

46:22.213 --> 46:23.581
(both grunting)

46:23.681 --> 46:26.151
(upbeat music)

46:29.687 --> 46:30.755
Come on.

46:30.856 --> 46:32.123
(both grunting)

46:32.223 --> 46:33.058
Hell!

46:40.431 --> 46:43.068
(upbeat music)

46:45.770 --> 46:46.471
Okay.

46:46.571 --> 46:48.006
Dylan?

46:48.106 --> 46:51.176
(Mom speaking in foreign
language)

46:51.276 --> 46:52.944
A video, mom.

46:53.044 --> 46:54.145
Sorry, Auntie.

46:54.245 --> 46:55.080
Habibi.

46:56.414 --> 46:57.682
Hello.

46:57.782 --> 47:00.451
- Is your friend staying
over? The bed is made.

47:00.551 --> 47:01.519
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

47:01.619 --> 47:02.988
She's just visiting.

47:03.221 --> 47:05.756
- And have either of you
offered her something to eat?

47:09.394 --> 47:12.763
Haram, well, Haram, who raised
your mama?

47:14.399 --> 47:15.333
Are you hungry?

47:18.103 --> 47:18.769
Yeah.

47:19.770 --> 47:22.007
(siren beeping)

47:22.107 --> 47:23.574
- The Cutlass belongs to Frankie
DeFranco.

47:23.674 --> 47:25.376
Ex-military was stationed in
Beirut

47:25.476 --> 47:27.545
during barracks bombing in '83.

47:27.645 --> 47:30.515
Says here she was discharged
after failing psych evaluation.

47:30.615 --> 47:32.017
Let me guess.

47:32.117 --> 47:34.185
She went AWOL the second
she saw some kid bleed out.

47:34.285 --> 47:37.555
- No, actually it says
she fired on bags of rice.

47:37.655 --> 47:41.492
- Huh? Frankie DeFranco
does not like risotto.

47:41.592 --> 47:42.493
[Mom] More rice.

47:42.693 --> 47:43.528
- [Dylan] More rice on her
plate.

47:43.628 --> 47:44.896
[Frankie] Mm mm mm mm.

47:44.996 --> 47:46.231
[Dylan] It's all really good.

47:46.464 --> 47:48.099
- This is the most amazing
thing I've ever tasted.

47:48.199 --> 47:49.534
Mm.

47:49.634 --> 47:50.335
What's this?

47:50.435 --> 47:51.236
Mm.

47:52.503 --> 47:53.504
And what's this?

47:53.604 --> 47:54.405
Pitha.

47:55.040 --> 47:56.174
And honestly,

47:56.674 --> 47:58.876
this doesn't even compare
to what you get over there.

47:58.977 --> 48:01.379
Oh no. It's really special.

48:01.479 --> 48:02.480
Wanna become a big actor

48:02.680 --> 48:04.715
and do my own stunts, like
Stallone.

48:04.815 --> 48:06.184
- He's gonna be like the
Lebanese Rocky.

48:06.284 --> 48:07.652
Yeah, I will.

48:07.852 --> 48:08.853
And I'm gonna show them what
Beirut is really made of.

48:08.954 --> 48:09.854
- You will.
- I will.

48:09.955 --> 48:11.022
Maybe I'll get to go someday.

48:11.222 --> 48:12.823
- Yo, you should come with us
next time.

48:13.791 --> 48:16.661
(Lebanese music)

48:18.063 --> 48:19.430
I bet Spooky would love it.

48:19.530 --> 48:20.831
Crystal and Minks, too.

48:25.236 --> 48:26.737
We have to get them outta there.

48:29.507 --> 48:30.942
Okay.

48:31.042 --> 48:32.410
If we're gonna get through this
alive,

48:32.510 --> 48:34.112
we need to know exactly what
we're doing

48:34.212 --> 48:35.080
and where we're going.

48:36.847 --> 48:38.449
Show us the lay of the land.

48:38.549 --> 48:40.385
(acoustic guitar music)

48:40.485 --> 48:41.352
Okay.

48:43.554 --> 48:45.090
Here is the main house,

48:45.190 --> 48:47.725
and then the shed is in the
back.

48:47.825 --> 48:48.960
It's pretty remote, there's only
one road

48:49.060 --> 48:49.927
that leads right to the front,

48:50.028 --> 48:51.662
so they'll see us coming.

48:51.762 --> 48:54.799
(knocking on door)

48:55.600 --> 48:57.335
Do you?

48:57.435 --> 48:58.436
- I don't know. Do you?
- No.

48:58.536 --> 48:59.737
(doorbell ringing)

48:59.837 --> 49:01.306
- Dylan!
- Okay, Mama.

49:06.177 --> 49:08.079
(Dylan muffled)

49:08.179 --> 49:09.447
Hi.

49:09.547 --> 49:10.281
- We're here to ask you
a few questions about-

49:10.381 --> 49:11.382
Do you speak American?

49:12.550 --> 49:14.619
- Yes sir, I do. I speak
three languages fluently.

49:14.719 --> 49:16.421
Are you Demeter?

49:16.521 --> 49:17.989
Yeah. I go by Dylan, but yeah.

49:18.089 --> 49:19.590
- I'm Officer Corbett. We're
here to ask-

49:19.690 --> 49:20.625
- We're looking for Frankie
DeFranco.

49:20.725 --> 49:21.892
You know where she is?

49:23.528 --> 49:26.297
- [Dylan] Seen her, is
there something wrong?

49:26.397 --> 49:28.499
- Would you mind if I take a
look around?

49:29.634 --> 49:31.802
- No, not not, not at all. Come
on in.

49:33.071 --> 49:35.573
(tense music)

49:42.447 --> 49:44.282
- [Kelly] How long have
you lived here for?

49:44.382 --> 49:47.052
- Oh, in America? About 10
years.

49:47.152 --> 49:48.653
- You live alone?
- No, I live, I live

49:48.753 --> 49:49.854
with my mom and my uncle

49:49.954 --> 49:51.522
And Frankie?

49:51.622 --> 49:55.393
- Frankie? Frankie, she usually
just drifts, drifts around.

49:55.493 --> 49:57.728
Last I heard she had a
place up on Division.

49:57.828 --> 49:59.297
- Division?
- Yeah.

49:59.397 --> 50:00.131
- [Kelly] Great, when was
the last time you saw her?

50:00.231 --> 50:01.399
Last time I saw her?

50:01.499 --> 50:02.867
Last time I saw her, two, two
weeks ago.

50:02.967 --> 50:04.235
A week ago, a week ago. Yeah.

50:04.335 --> 50:06.171
She was at my uncle's
restaurant.

50:06.271 --> 50:08.473
Habibi Cafe and lounge.

50:08.573 --> 50:11.342
- H-A-B-I.
- Yeah, B-I.

50:12.643 --> 50:14.945
(tense music)

50:22.587 --> 50:24.955
(door opening)

50:29.927 --> 50:33.131
(tense music continues)

50:49.880 --> 50:53.184
(tense music continues)

51:07.832 --> 51:08.733
Can I help you?

51:08.833 --> 51:09.467
Shit.

51:09.567 --> 51:10.801
(teapot crashing)

51:10.901 --> 51:12.270
Goddamn it.

51:12.370 --> 51:14.372
- I'm really, sorry. Are you
okay?

51:14.472 --> 51:15.540
Please, let me help you.

51:15.640 --> 51:16.574
No, don't.

51:16.674 --> 51:17.608
You want a banana?

51:17.708 --> 51:18.576
- It's really-
- No, I'm fine.

51:18.676 --> 51:20.278
It's from my brother, then.

51:20.378 --> 51:22.780
Trust me. No, thank you.

51:22.880 --> 51:23.914
- It will help with your
indigestion.

51:24.014 --> 51:25.450
She hurt me with her tea.

51:25.550 --> 51:26.617
The orange blossom tea?

51:28.186 --> 51:28.986
Goddamn it, lady.

51:29.086 --> 51:30.020
I don't know what's wrong

51:30.321 --> 51:32.022
with your fucking ears, but I
said no.

51:34.659 --> 51:37.428
- You come into my house, poking
around.

51:37.528 --> 51:39.664
You did not even say hello.
I offer you something.

51:39.764 --> 51:40.765
I think it's

51:40.865 --> 51:41.499
- time to go.
- Something I made

51:41.599 --> 51:42.433
with my own hands.

51:42.533 --> 51:43.301
And you say (indistinct).

51:45.270 --> 51:46.271
[Dylan] Mom.

51:47.572 --> 51:48.439
Goddamn foreigners.

51:50.074 --> 51:54.279
(Mom speaking in foreign
language)

51:57.114 --> 52:00.351
- Thank you, let us know
if you need anything else.

52:00.451 --> 52:04.121
(Mom and Dylan speaking
in foreign language)

52:04.222 --> 52:05.523
They're gone.

52:05.623 --> 52:08.058
(tense music)

52:11.629 --> 52:12.763
We're fucked.

52:15.733 --> 52:18.236
(tense music)

52:36.821 --> 52:38.223
Oh, you're back.

52:38.323 --> 52:40.090
- Yeah. I need to do a bit of
recon.

52:41.459 --> 52:43.093
Pam, I'll be fine. You should go
home.

52:44.462 --> 52:45.830
Okay.

52:45.930 --> 52:47.632
Before you go,

52:47.732 --> 52:49.099
are these all of Breaker's
cases?

52:50.968 --> 52:52.102
All the ones he turned in.

52:53.671 --> 52:56.407
(eerie music)

52:56.507 --> 52:57.408
Goodnight.

52:57.508 --> 52:58.709
See you later.

53:00.478 --> 53:03.113
(sinister music)

53:21.131 --> 53:24.635
(sinister music continues)

53:42.687 --> 53:46.156
(sinister music continues)

54:06.877 --> 54:07.712
Bingo.

54:12.750 --> 54:15.520
(phone ringing)

54:19.156 --> 54:19.957
Hey.

54:20.891 --> 54:21.726
Hello?

54:23.260 --> 54:24.094
Goldie?

54:26.731 --> 54:27.698
You know,

54:31.268 --> 54:35.072
most people are average

54:35.172 --> 54:37.408
because they don't know the
difference

54:37.508 --> 54:40.711
between inconvenience and
opportunity.

54:43.280 --> 54:44.782
- What the hell is that supposed
to mean?

54:44.882 --> 54:47.618
- It means that I'm making
lemonade

54:47.718 --> 54:48.819
and you can't have any.

54:50.220 --> 54:52.657
You're out Billy Boy, it's over.

54:52.757 --> 54:54.158
Cut the bullshit.

54:54.258 --> 54:56.494
There wouldn't be a deal
if it weren't for me.

54:56.594 --> 54:59.129
- Precisely, yet I can't
think of a single reason

54:59.229 --> 55:00.297
why I need you anymore.

55:01.766 --> 55:05.035
Enough snow to cancel
school for a year, right?

55:05.135 --> 55:07.104
- You got it back.
- Something like that.

55:07.204 --> 55:10.107
- Goddamn it Goldie, I did
everything you asked of me.

55:10.207 --> 55:12.877
Okay, I brought the deal to the
table. You can't cut me out.

55:12.977 --> 55:15.012
Oh, come on Billy.

55:15.112 --> 55:18.282
Did you really think that I
would let you leave me first?

55:18.383 --> 55:20.485
Good luck with that retirement,
now.

55:21.586 --> 55:23.454
- I'm gonna fuckin' hang
you, do you hear me?

55:23.554 --> 55:24.989
You're fuckin' dead.

55:25.089 --> 55:26.724
Fuckin' bitch.

55:26.824 --> 55:30.428
(dramatic instrumental music)

55:34.999 --> 55:37.368
(Spooky crying)

55:56.954 --> 56:00.290
(dramatic music continues)

56:10.935 --> 56:13.303
(door closing)

56:15.873 --> 56:18.308
(siren blaring)

56:25.816 --> 56:28.318
(music fading)

56:34.024 --> 56:36.393
(door slamming)

56:55.345 --> 56:57.081
Why you little bitch.

56:59.550 --> 57:00.985
I'll take you all down.

57:01.085 --> 57:03.921
(dramatic music)

57:08.325 --> 57:09.093
[Fox] It's not gonna work.

57:10.728 --> 57:11.929
That cop works for Goldie.

57:15.265 --> 57:18.135
I'm not walking you guys
into a suicide mission.

57:18.235 --> 57:19.069
They'll kill you.

57:20.505 --> 57:21.305
Maybe.

57:22.773 --> 57:24.141
Better me than the girls,

57:24.241 --> 57:25.910
(Frankie groaning)

57:26.010 --> 57:26.811
or my sister.

57:28.012 --> 57:28.813
You can't go.

57:30.047 --> 57:32.550
(pensive music)

57:39.757 --> 57:42.493
- Okay, hold on. Goldie has one
dirty cop.

57:44.595 --> 57:46.664
Big whoop, we can still take
them.

57:46.764 --> 57:48.866
No, you don't know this guy.

57:48.966 --> 57:50.400
He'll do anything for a payday.

57:52.770 --> 57:54.038
I should have known she
was gonna get him involved

57:54.138 --> 57:55.139
when I took the bag.

57:55.906 --> 57:57.508
What bag?

57:57.608 --> 57:59.777
- I accidentally swiped a
duffle bag full of blow.

58:01.912 --> 58:03.480
(Frankie and Dylan chuckling)

58:03.581 --> 58:06.150
In my defense, I thought it was
money.

58:09.219 --> 58:10.354
What?

58:10.454 --> 58:12.790
You've just been walking around

58:12.890 --> 58:15.693
with an industrial amount of
cocaine?

58:15.793 --> 58:17.161
No.

58:17.261 --> 58:18.295
No, of course not.

58:19.329 --> 58:20.164
I stashed it.

58:23.634 --> 58:25.570
(Dylan's fingers snapping)

58:25.670 --> 58:26.503
This is good.

58:27.838 --> 58:28.939
This is great.

58:30.808 --> 58:31.642
Cobra?

58:34.078 --> 58:35.813
- I don't know. I haven't seen
it.

58:37.648 --> 58:41.719
- This is a classic hostage
negotiation situation.

58:41.819 --> 58:43.420
They have something we want.

58:43.520 --> 58:44.822
We have something they want.

58:44.922 --> 58:46.190
Yes.

58:46.290 --> 58:48.192
- We can't just walk up to the
front door.

58:48.292 --> 58:49.760
I mean, we've been made.

58:49.860 --> 58:51.328
Not all of us have been made.

58:54.364 --> 58:55.499
We even have the getaway car.

58:57.134 --> 58:59.036
(rock music)

58:59.136 --> 59:00.437
This is Boss,

59:00.537 --> 59:02.607
she was a gift from my
dad on my 18th birthday.

59:02.707 --> 59:04.474
My uncle brought her over from
Beirut.

59:07.144 --> 59:07.712
Are you sure?

59:10.047 --> 59:12.482
(upbeat music)

59:24.028 --> 59:25.529
(car starting)

59:25.630 --> 59:29.033
(engine revving)

59:29.133 --> 59:31.501
(engine dying)

59:33.704 --> 59:37.608
- (foreign phrase) She's,
she's just warming up.

59:37.708 --> 59:39.710
She's hot, she's getting warm.

59:39.810 --> 59:41.278
- Okay, great.
(car starting)

59:41.378 --> 59:42.546
- Yeah.
- There we go.

59:42.647 --> 59:44.982
(tires squealing)

59:45.082 --> 59:48.152
(engine revving)

59:48.252 --> 59:50.520
(upbeat music)

59:56.894 --> 59:58.228
(knocking on door)

59:58.428 --> 01:00:02.066
- Sergeant Billy Breaker.
Open up, we need to talk.

01:00:02.166 --> 01:00:04.568
(rock music)

01:00:07.672 --> 01:00:08.472
- [Billy] Come on, come on, come
on.

01:00:11.208 --> 01:00:13.778
(laughing) There you are.

01:00:16.013 --> 01:00:18.415
(rock music)

01:00:25.289 --> 01:00:26.123
You ready?

01:00:27.057 --> 01:00:29.559
(rock music)

01:00:47.311 --> 01:00:49.179
(door closing)

01:00:49.279 --> 01:00:50.314
I have some bad news.

01:00:52.082 --> 01:00:53.150
- Fuck.
- Yeah.

01:00:53.751 --> 01:00:56.020
But I do have some good news.
I do have some good news.

01:00:56.453 --> 01:00:59.589
I come prepared.

01:01:00.324 --> 01:01:01.158
Huh?

01:01:05.495 --> 01:01:06.530
Seriously.

01:01:11.135 --> 01:01:13.603
(tense music)

01:01:29.086 --> 01:01:32.056
(uptempo dance music)

01:02:04.955 --> 01:02:07.657
(engine rumbling)

01:02:09.960 --> 01:02:10.660
Let's go.

01:02:13.730 --> 01:02:16.266
(engine stops)

01:02:24.508 --> 01:02:26.844
- Hey, what is this an
interrogation?

01:02:28.078 --> 01:02:28.678
Come on.

01:02:29.679 --> 01:02:31.415
Who are you, asshole?

01:02:31.515 --> 01:02:33.784
Who am I, asshole?

01:02:33.884 --> 01:02:36.086
I'm the asshole that has friends
downtown

01:02:36.186 --> 01:02:39.223
that says you two boys might
need something that I have.

01:02:40.490 --> 01:02:41.425
- What the?
- So let me just start

01:02:41.525 --> 01:02:43.227
from the beginning of the story.

01:02:47.231 --> 01:02:50.434
(dance music continues)

01:02:57.942 --> 01:02:59.243
Fox, is it you?

01:03:00.845 --> 01:03:02.446
I need you to be quiet.

01:03:02.546 --> 01:03:03.247
What do you mean, me?

01:03:03.347 --> 01:03:04.481
Minx, she's back.

01:03:04.581 --> 01:03:05.782
Okay, we gotta go

01:03:05.883 --> 01:03:07.784
and I need you guys to come with
me.

01:03:07.885 --> 01:03:09.453
Where the hell have you been?

01:03:09.553 --> 01:03:11.255
I've been a sinner.

01:03:11.355 --> 01:03:12.156
What's in the bag?

01:03:12.356 --> 01:03:13.357
But I ain't no crook, okay?

01:03:13.457 --> 01:03:14.158
I'm not a crook.

01:03:14.258 --> 01:03:15.325
Come on, huh?

01:03:15.425 --> 01:03:17.061
I'm just trying to get to the
big

01:03:19.229 --> 01:03:20.931
pasta and fazul up in the sky.

01:03:21.031 --> 01:03:21.999
Y'all know what I mean?

01:03:24.301 --> 01:03:26.236
- I never heard no gumba say,
y'all.

01:03:28.538 --> 01:03:29.539
Take it easy, okay?

01:03:29.639 --> 01:03:30.975
Because I-

01:03:31.075 --> 01:03:34.111
- You walking in like nothing
happened.

01:03:34.211 --> 01:03:35.145
Shit!

01:03:35.245 --> 01:03:36.346
(ominous music)

01:03:36.446 --> 01:03:41.485
Fuck!
(gun firing)

01:03:41.818 --> 01:03:43.153
(Domino grunting)

01:03:43.253 --> 01:03:45.322
Oh, come on Fox.

01:03:45.422 --> 01:03:47.457
You don't want me to
accidentally shoot Minx, now do you?

01:03:47.557 --> 01:03:49.960
(gun firing)

01:03:54.264 --> 01:03:55.099
Okay.

01:03:57.501 --> 01:03:59.536
Welcome home darling.

01:03:59.636 --> 01:04:00.971
Fuck you, asshole.

01:04:01.071 --> 01:04:03.473
(gun firing)

01:04:04.741 --> 01:04:06.243
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.

01:04:06.343 --> 01:04:07.912
Fuck you.

01:04:08.012 --> 01:04:09.579
- Atta girl, stick it to her
like fuckin' Chinese chicken.

01:04:09.679 --> 01:04:12.349
I'm Japanese you dumb duck.

01:04:12.449 --> 01:04:14.818
(all grunting)

01:04:17.287 --> 01:04:19.323
- I know you're mad, but
I had to get my sister.

01:04:19.423 --> 01:04:20.357
(gun firing)

01:04:20.457 --> 01:04:21.025
- Oh.
- Let's go.

01:04:23.527 --> 01:04:24.561
(Ricky growling)

01:04:24.661 --> 01:04:25.529
We're supposed to be sisters.

01:04:25.629 --> 01:04:26.696
We are.

01:04:26.796 --> 01:04:28.665
Then, why did you leave?

01:04:28.765 --> 01:04:32.002
(somber music)

01:04:32.102 --> 01:04:35.039
Come on, come on guys.

01:04:35.139 --> 01:04:36.740
We gotta go.

01:04:36.840 --> 01:04:39.043
You gotta get us out of here.

01:04:39.143 --> 01:04:39.843
Come on.

01:04:39.944 --> 01:04:41.845
(somber music)

01:04:41.946 --> 01:04:43.547
[Ricky] Come here.

01:04:44.614 --> 01:04:45.882
Sisters in blood.

01:04:48.385 --> 01:04:50.988
(others grunting)

01:04:52.522 --> 01:04:54.824
(rock music)

01:04:57.394 --> 01:05:00.430
- Go to the gas station. Stay
there, I'll meet you there.

01:05:00.530 --> 01:05:02.366
I'm right behind you.

01:05:02.466 --> 01:05:03.200
What about you?

01:05:03.300 --> 01:05:04.068
I have to get Spooky.

01:05:04.168 --> 01:05:05.035
- I'll be fine.
- Okay.

01:05:06.903 --> 01:05:09.773
(both growling and grunting)

01:05:09.873 --> 01:05:11.541
[Dylan] Commando.

01:05:11.641 --> 01:05:13.043
[Domino] Fuck Commando.

01:05:13.143 --> 01:05:15.845
(Domino grunting)

01:05:20.384 --> 01:05:21.218
Here please!

01:05:23.853 --> 01:05:24.888
Fox.

01:05:24.989 --> 01:05:26.323
Hey.

01:05:26.423 --> 01:05:29.026
(Ricky grunting)

01:05:30.360 --> 01:05:35.132
Dylan!

01:05:35.232 --> 01:05:37.867
(Domino growling)

01:05:39.569 --> 01:05:42.906
